    at rate `unruhPeriod a`. So the ONE `β` fixed by the geometric return-surface closure (N360) is the
    reciprocal-temperature rate of the statistical equilibrium (N375) — the acceleration–temperature tie
    is the co-occurrence of the two banked modules, not a field-quantization posit. -/
theorem unruh_kms_equilibrium {n : ℕ} [NeZero n] (E : Fin n → Cut) (a : Cut) :
    ∃ c, MaxEnt.IsGibbsState (MaxEnt.boltzmann E (unruhPeriod a)) E (unruhPeriod a) c :=
  ⟨_, MaxEnt.boltzmann_isGibbs E (unruhPeriod a)⟩

/-- ★ THE ONE `β` (the weld stated as a triple): the SAME `β = unruhPeriod a` is (1) the geometric
    closure period `a·β = azimuthalTurn`; (2) the reciprocal of the temperature `T = a/(2·cutPi)`; and
    (3) the reciprocal-temperature rate of the banked C6-forced maxent equilibrium. Geometry (arc E),
    thermality, and statistics (arc G) meet in one derived number. -/
theorem unruh_period_is_kms_rate {n : ℕ} [NeZero n] (E : Fin n → Cut) (a : Cut) (ha : a ≠ 0) :
    (a * unruhPeriod a = azimuthalTurn)
      ∧ (unruhTemp a = a / (2 * cutPi))
      ∧ (∃ c, MaxEnt.IsGibbsState (MaxEnt.boltzmann E (unruhPeriod a)) E (unruhPeriod a) c) :=
  ⟨unruh_closure a ha, unruhTemp_eq a, unruh_kms_equilibrium E a⟩

/-! ## (5) THE HEART bundled. -/

/-- ★★★ THE UNRUH / KMS-MODULAR WELD (the capstone): the Rindler-orbit Euclidean section CLOSES under
    the full KMS period `unruhPeriod a` (the fold's return-surface closure) and NOT under a half-turn
